\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Run on Corpbank prompts \uc2 Bulgarian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to seize control\b0\par\par\uc2 1,054 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2014\par 20:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Follows reports of shady deals involving top shareholder\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take control for three months\par \par \uc2 * Says no fear of contagion to other lenders\par \par \uc2 * Hungary's OTP, Greece's NBG both say no impact on ops\par \par \uc2 * Bulgarian credit default swaps rise to 6-month high (Adds banker and depositor quotes, details, background, market close)\par \par \uc2 By Matthias Williams and Tsvetelia Tsolova\par \par \uc2 SOFIA, June 20 (Reuters) - A run on \uc2 Corporate Commercial Bank\uc2  (Corpbank) prompted \uc2 Bulgaria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take control of the country's fourth-largest lender on Friday and its governor appealed to depositors to stay calm.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bulgarian National Bank\uc2  (BNB) said it would handle Corpbank's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for three months and removed its management and supervisory board after the run, which was sparked by media reports of shady deals involving the bank.\par \par \uc2 The BNB said it acted after Corpbank said on Friday morning it had stopped all payments and bank \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to a liquidity drain. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Corpbank was not bankrupt and other lenders in the country were safe from the effects.\par \par \uc2 "As you know, there has been a lot of talk about the bank and one of its shareholders, which triggered bank runs," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Ivan Iskrov\uc2  said at a news conference. "It is very important to be very careful when we talk about banks. Let's not tear down our house alone unnecessarily."\par \par \uc2 "Let me make this very clear. \uc2 Corporate Commercial Bank\uc2  is not a bankrupt bank. We are acting swiftly to avoid a bankruptcy," said Iskrov.\par \par \uc2 He declined to give further details of the bank's problems and said supervisors would carry out a full audit of its books.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action did not stop dozens of people from queuing outside the main office of the bank in the capital Sofia on Friday, and credit default swaps on the country's debt hit a six-month high on fears of contagion. Sofia's blue-chip shares index closed at its lowest level since February.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  blocked depositors from withdrawing cash after it took control.\par \par \uc2 "We are worried, because my husband and I have deposits there in euros and in U.S. dollars," said Lilia Polova, editor at a lifestyle magazine. "These are our family savings. He was reading newspapers and was asking me to take our money out of there ... but I waited."\par \par \uc2 Bulgaria's stock exchange suspended Corpbank from trading and the country's financial regulator ordered that the shares remain suspended until Wednesday next week in order to protect investors and stabilise the market.\par \par \uc2 LETTER LEAKED\par \par \uc2 Iskrov said Corpbank depositors stepped up withdrawals after an anonymous letter leaked to Bulgarian media said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor in charge of banking supervision was being investigated by prosecutors for abuse of office.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since confirmed the investigation and said the deputy governor had taken a voluntary leave of absence.\par \par \uc2 Reports in Bulgarian media linked the investigation of the deputy governor to allegations of corruption at Corpbank.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with a Bulgarian TV news channel, whose contents were published by Corpbank on Thursday, Corpbank's top shareholder Tsvetan Vassilev denied any wrongdoing on his part or the bank's.\par \par \uc2 "We are a responsible bank both towards our client depositors and Bulgarian business," he said. Corpbank said on Thursday that Vassilev was ready to cooperate with the investigation into the bank's affairs.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Corpbank said on Friday that she was not allowed to make statements without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's approval. She said she did not know Vassilev's whereabouts and in any case would not be allowed to share such information.\par \par \uc2 The leading shareholders in the Sofia-listed bank are Vassilev, with just over half the company, Oman's sovereign wealth fund with around 30 percent and Russia's VTB Asset Management with nearly 10 percent, Thomson Reuters data showed.\par \par \uc2 Friday's move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the first such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1996-1997 financial crisis, which led to the bankruptcies of 14 Bulgarian banks and forced the introduction of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board regime in the country.\par \par \uc2 SITUATION "ISOLATED"\par \par \uc2 The bank run comes at a bad time for Bulgaria's government, which is preparing for an early election after the ruling Socialists suffered a bad result in \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  elections and a junior coalition partner withdrew its support.\par \par \uc2 Political instability in the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's poorest state has smothered reforms needed to spur economic growth and tackle high employment. \uc2 Standard and Poor's\uc2  downgraded Bulgaria's sovereign credit ratings last week to a notch above junk.\par \par \uc2 The government said it was ready to support efforts to stabilise Corpbank. Shareholder VTB also expressed interest in lending support, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said talks with VTB would start immediately.\par \par \uc2 Iskrov was quick to play down concerns that the panic could spread to other lenders in the region, which sits on the edge of a euro zone still recovering from its own financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 He said Bulgaria's banking system was not interlinked enough for Corpbank's problems to spread.\par \par \uc2 There are 29 commercial banks operating in Bulgaria and some three quarters of the banking system's assets are foreign-owned. Among foreign banks with \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Bulgaria are \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  , \uc2 Raiffeisen Bank\uc2 , Hungary's OTP, \uc2 National Bank of Greece\uc2 , Eurobank and \uc2 Alpha Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 OTP said the situation was "isolated", and \uc2 National Bank of Greece\uc2  and Eurobank both said their Bulgarian units were not experiencing any problems.\par \par \uc2 Bulgarian bank deposits in local and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are guaranteed up to 196,000 levs ($136,600), or 100,000 euros by law. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will launch talks with shareholders to calculate the support the bank will need, Iskrov said.\par \par \uc2 "There is no spillover effect. I think that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government take fast measures there will be none," said Levon Hampartzoumian, chief executive of Unicredit Bulbank, Bulgaria's largest lender and head of the Association of Commercial Banks in Bulgaria.\par \par \uc2 "There is no similarity to the 1996 crisis, when there were serious cross-banking exposures," he told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 1.4349 Bulgarian Levs) (Writing by Pravin Char and Simon Jessop; editing by Tom Pfeiffer) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-20T19:22:24.000Z   \par \par