\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4-Poland  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 ,  \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria \highlight\uc2  ERM-2 delay hit  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 936 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2010\par 16:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Zloty knocked down by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2  drops ERM-2 entry plans, mkt spooked\par \par \uc2 * Investors in wait-and-see mode ahead of Hungary election\par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout)\par \par \uc2 By Marius Zaharia and Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST/WARSAW, April 9 (Reuters) - The zloty fell on Friday after the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 10 years, while other central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were pressured by Bulgaria's decision to delay its euro plans after revealing a hidden budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement it bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, following a string of comments from officials this week trying to talk the zloty down. [ID:nWSF008905] [ID:nLDE63806P]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor Witold Kozinski said later in the day the bank could not rule out further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. [ID:nWSF008910]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised concerns that policymakers in other central European countries might favour undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help economies recover from their worst recession in decades.\par \par \uc2 "There is a sentiment others will do the same as Poland. Romania has already done it and now investors are encouraged to think more ... is to come," a dealer in Bucharest said.\par \par \uc2 Another case of regional contagion occurred after Bulgaria announced it was delaying plans to enter the ERM-2 euro entry waiting zone because of unaccounted procurement deals that have widened the deficit to 3.7 percent of GDP last year from an initial 1.9 percent gap. [ID:nLDE63813A] [ID:nLDE63813L]\par \par \uc2 Dealers in Romania said investors became concerned that other countries in central Europe could have hidden deficits like Greece, and the leu was worst hit by the Bulgarian news. [ID:nBUC003670]\par \par \uc2 "Obviously, we may see a deterioration of investor sentiment. We've already seen an impact on the leu," said Melania Hancila, chief economist at Volksbank in Bucharest.\par \par \uc2 "I do believe that investors will be very carefully assessing data coming from Romania and other countries in the region. CDS quotations may rise because of this situation in Bulgaria."\par \par \uc2 At 1413 GMT, the zloty <EURPLN=> was down 0.6 percent at 3.871 per euro, off almost two-week lows hit earlier in the session.\par \par \uc2 The leu <EURRON=> was down 0.5 percent, while the Czech crown <EURCZK=> was almost flat and Hungary's forint <EURHUF=> gained 0.3 percent from Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY'S ELECTION\par \par \uc2 Hungarians will vote on Sunday in the first round of an election that looks set to bring a landslide victory for the opposition centre-right Fidesz party, giving it a strong mandate for reforms. [ID:nLDE6351AW]\par \par \uc2 Fidesz, which campaigned on tax cuts and job creation, could even secure a two-thirds majority, which would empower the party to pass broader structural reforms.\par \par \uc2 "The market is in a wait-and-see mode," one trader in Budapest said. "Indications for a chance of a two-thirds majority (for opposition party Fidesz) on Sunday could reassure markets and be mildly forint positive."\par \par \uc2 Hungarian bonds were steady, and analysts say their bull run may continue after the election as an expected strong majority government, a supply squeeze and hopes for more rate cuts bode well [ID:nLDE62U1OZ].\par \par \uc2 The forint, however, is set to give up some ground in the next few months after the elections, a monthly Reuters poll showed on Friday, but is poised for a modest gain of less than 1 percent over a 12-month horizon.[ID:nLDE6380S7]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2009 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>  25.187   25.195   +0.03%   +4.49%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>   3.871    3.847   -0.62%   +6.02%\par Hungarian forint <EURHUF=> 266.55   267.36    +0.3%    +1.43%\par Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>   7.27     7.27       0%    +0.54%\par Romanian leu     <EURRON=>   4.133    4.114   -0.46%   +2.53%\par Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>  99.61    99.61        0%   -3.74%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=>\par 3-yr T-bond   CZ3YT=RR    -11 basis points to  63bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR    -5 basis points to  +83bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR    -5 basis points to  +75bps over bmk*\par Polish treasury bonds <0#PLBMK=>\par 2-yr T-bond   PL2YT=RR    -5 basis points to  +350bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   PL5YT=RR    -6 basis points to  +295bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond PL10YT=RR    -5 basis points to  +245bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds <0#HUBMK=>\par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR    -7 basis points to  +458bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU