\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Bulgaria c.bank says FIBank in "excellent condition"\b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2008\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, FIBank comment, paragraphs 5-8)\par \par \uc2 SOFIA, May 16 (Reuters) - Bulgaria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said First Investment Bank (FIBank) and other Bulgarian banks were in "excellent condition", dismissing rumours it faced financial problems.\par \par \uc2 Rumours have spread via several Bulgarian Internet blogs in the past two weeks that FIBank, Bulgaria's sixth largest bank by assets, had problems. That led to deposit withdrawals in the past few days, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 "The governing board of the BNB (Bulgaria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) categorically confirms that all Bulgarian banks, including FIBank are in an excellent condition with high liquidity and normal credit levels," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "The BNB will not allow FIBank to fall into trouble on the basis of unfounded rumours," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 FIBank said a separate statement later on Friday that deposit withdrawals, which surged in the past two days, had now fallen sharply.\par \par \uc2 "The crisis caused by the rumours has been overcome and client trust in the bank will recover in the next few days," said the bank, most of which is privately held, said.\par \par \uc2 Local news agency Focus quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Ivan Iskrov as saying that the spread of the rumours was a "scenario" aiming at damaging FIBank's credibility.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will ask prosecutors to investigate the case, Iskrov said.\par \par \uc2 Bulgarians still have bitter memories of a 1996/97 financial crisis that wiped out a third of the Balkan country's banks. The European Union newcomer has since introduced a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board regime that pegs the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the euro.\par \par \uc2 FIBank had assets worth of 4.07 billion levs ($3.22 billion) at end-March, when it posted a net profit of 15.07 million levs up from 10.1 million profit a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Bulgarian banks have enjoyed a credit boom in the past few years as people sought debt to buy consumer goods like flat screen TVs, new cars and houses after decades of communist austerity.\par \par \uc2 Loans grew 62.5 percent last year, while deposits rose by 34.3 percent, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , worried by the credit boom, urged banks late last year to raise lending rates and tighten rules. It has said it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with fresh measures to cool the trend.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 29 banks are mainly owned by big European lenders, many from Italy, Austria, Germany and Greece. (Reporting by Anna Mudeva and Tsvetelia Ilieva; editing by Rory Channing)\par \par \uc2 FIBANK-BULGARIA/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|GNN|M|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080516e45g001jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
