\par\par \b \uc2  Bulgaria lev slumps to 575-585 per dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SOFIA, Jan 3 (Reuter) - The Bulgarian lev slumped to 575-585 per dollar in low interbank volume on the first trading day of 1997 from 507-510 at the close on December 30 as foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand heavily topped supply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "A commercial bank and a financial house have been aggressively bidding for dollars since the opening, buying every dollar on offer irrespective of the ask price," a commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was bid around 595 levs around 1030 local time (0830 GMT), but no one offered foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below 610, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were unsure whether financial institutions bought dollars for final clients or built up \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions in anticipation of a pending sharp lev fall in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) was not seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by mid-morning, traders said. BNB officials were not available for comment \par \par \uc2  BNB governor Lyubomir Filipov said on Sunday that BNB powers to counter pressure on the lev through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were limited because payments on \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign debt in 1997 would be a priority for the BNB. @ \par \par \uc2  Low BNB \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, lack of financing from abroad and lower than expected privatisation proceeds in 1996 were the reasons why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not prevent a lev decline, Filipov said. \par \par \uc2  Filipov said Bulgaria has to pay some $170-180 million coupon on its Brady bonds on January 28. \par \par \uc2  BNB \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $525 million at the end of November last year. \par \par \uc2  -- Anastas Petrov, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-876032 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt1304j4o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
