\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 BULGARIA \highlight\uc2  LEV WEAKENS AS C.BANK FAILS TO  \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SOFIA, Dec 4 (Reuter) - The Bulgarian lev closed at a new all-time low of 415-418 per dollar after 395-400 in the morning as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNB) was not seen supporting it amid a persistently high foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Fuel importers were bidding for relatively large dollar volumes but supply from banks was low and the lev lost some 30 (levs per dollar) on the day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  BNB officials declined comment. \par \par \uc2  The lev closed around 386-387 on Tuesday on the interbank market. It traded at 362-364 per dollar on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Commercial banks were reluctant to sell dollars in anticipation of a further lev fall amid unsatisfied foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand from final clients, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the exchange rate was not moved by a BNB decisison on Wednesday to continue to participate on the local market to support the lev. \par \par \uc2  "The BNB does not have much room left to prevent a lev slide through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its reserves fell again last month," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  BNB \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $15.7 million to $525.1 million in November, the BNB said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Reserves stood near $1.41 billion in November 1995 and have steadily declined since then due to payments on \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign debt and BNB \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the lev. \par \par \uc2  The BNB also said on Wednesday it had decided to step up supervision to ensure that commercial banks adhere to its regulations requiring banks to have a maximum ratio of 30 percent between their net open foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions and their own funds. \par \par \uc2  The previous low for the lev of 395 per dollar was on November 21. The lev traded near 70 to the dollar at the beginning of 1996. -- Anastas Petrov, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-876032 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040129dsc40096c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
