\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria \highlight\uc2  c.bank says  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  continue. \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SOFIA, Dec 4 (Reuter) - The Bulgarian National Bank said in a statement on Wednesday it will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the slumping lev. \par \par \uc2  The cash-strapped \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has carried out modest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the past month to prop up the lev, which fell from 246 to the dollar on November 4 to a record low 413 per dollar on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "In order to support the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BNB will continue to participate on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said the statement. \par \par \uc2  The BNB board, which will continue its session on Thursday, is also expected to step up supervision to ensure that commercial banks adhere to regulations requiring banks to have a maximum ratio of up to 30 percent between their net open foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions and their own funds, said the statement. \par \par \uc2  Bulgaria is currently debating the introduction of a tight financial regime, called a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, to resolve a grave economic crisis caused by delayed reform and siphoning of capital abroad. -- Elisaveta Konstantinova, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dsc402nhi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2