\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 BULGARIA \highlight\uc2  LEV SLUMPS AS C.BANK HALTS  \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SOFIA, Nov 20 (Reuter) - The Bulgarian lev slumped to 330-335 per dollar from 229 in the morning after foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply thinned down to a trickle and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the lev, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The (interbank) market was listless in the afternoon because most traders retreated to the sidelines after the lev nosedived to 330-335," a commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said an insurance company was bidding for large foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volumes for pending payments of dollar-denominated reinsurance fees, strongly pressuring the lev amid an almost non-existing dollar supply. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the lev like it was doing for most of November so far, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, who asked not to be identified, told Reuters the bank planned to save its dwindling \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the possible introduction of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board and for foreign debt payments rather than for propping up the lev. \par \par \uc2  Additional pressure over the lev came from the cash market, where Bulgarians converted lev savings into hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was offered at 345-350 levs at exchange bureaux in early afternoon, but lack of demand at these levels made sellers lower their asks for the dollar to 325-330 levs later on, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Individuals have withdrawn some 13 billion levs from the State Savings Bank since the middle of last week until Tuesday, part of which were probably channeled to the cash \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Bistra Dimitrova, head of the SSB told Reuters. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNB) \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves reserves stood near $541 million at the end of October, down from $1.434 billion a year ago, BNB figures show. \par \par \uc2  Apart from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages gold reserves worth some $400 million. \par \par \uc2  Dues to government and bank creditors in the first quarter of 1997 total $300 million or some 30 percent of all debt payments for next year. \par \par \uc2  A month ago BNB experts estimated Bulgaria would need some $200-300 million for fuel and food imports by the year-end. -- Anastas Petrov, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-876032 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040129dsbk006nn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
