\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Bulgaria - May 6. \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  These are some of the main stories in Sofia newspapers today. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  24 CHASA \par \par \uc2  The cabinet is expected to replace 100 of the 1063 firms on the mass sell-off list at an extraordinary session on Tuesday, the head of the Mass Privatisation Centre Kalin Mitrev said. @ \par \par \uc2  Bulgaria's foreign debt fell by $917 million to $9.445 billion in 1995 after debts to Russian commercial banks were settled, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its annual report. Bulgaria owes $5.4 to commercial creditors and $1.7 billion to international lending institutions. \par \par \uc2  Some firms, which are expected to be put on the liquidation list under a government programme, might be saved, the head of the Economic bank Plamen Petrov said. He referred to the Rousse-based shipyard, saying its creditors -- four Bulgarian banks -- might agree to extend fresh funding, because its ships had markets in Europe. \par \par \uc2  New car sales in Bulgaria dropped by nine percent to 1955 units year-on-year in the first quarter of this year, the Car Importers' Union said. \par \par \uc2  TROUD \par \par \uc2  Bulgarian banks' losses rose by 10.5 billion levs to 45.3 billion levs in February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The 16th International Spring Fair opens in the city of Plovdiv today with a record high number of firms taking part - 1485 from 44 countries. \par \par \uc2  PARI \par \par \uc2  The government was asked to take $550 million foreign debt of the state-owned Economic bank and Mineralbank to speed up restructuring in the banking sector and clear the way for fresh funding deals with official creditors, the heads of the two banks and Bulbank said in a letter to the government. \par \par \uc2  Bulgaria's private  Mollov commercial bank posted of 15 million levs profit in 1995, figures from its profit and loss account showed. \par \par \uc2  STANDART \par \par \uc2  Nine large banks have agreed to back the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in supprort of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the lev, by joint \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Association of Commercial Banks might split over proposed amendments to statutes, due to be discussed at a annual meeting on Tuesday. Under the amendments banks should have a number of votes proportional to their capital. At the moment each member bank has one vote, regardless of its capital. -- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-328101 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds5608jbx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
