\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria \highlight\uc2  Lev/Dollar -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Not  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 1996\par 12:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried twice this year to stop the steep rise of the dollar and protect the savings in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by raising the base interest rate to 49% currently from 34% at the end of last year. \par \par \uc2  But hopes that interest in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would fade and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in control were dashed. 'Our country needs \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for payments and to buy goods,' Varbarnov said. \par \par \uc2  Bankers maintain that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary measures are ineffective and that other financial mechanisms have to be found. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday or Wednesday, and Varbarnov said it's indicated that it won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  'because it doesn't have money for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  Official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped to around $900 million early this year from $1.2 billion at the end of 1995; they dropped further to $700 million at the end of March in part as Bulgaria made a regular payment to the commercial and official creditors under agreements. \par \par \uc2  Bulgaria owes some $1.2 billion in 1996 in principle and interest repayments. Officials expect a trade surplus of around $400 million and a current account surplus of $100 million in 1996. \par \par \uc2  'On this basis we hope in the spring and the summer to improve our reserves,' Filipov said. \par \par \uc2  The lev's depreciation reflects the difficulties which Bulgaria meets while trying to reform its communist-built economy along market lines. 'The big problem is in the economy,' Varbarnov said. While he said he thinks the government will be able to carry out its restructuring plans, 'this is very difficult and will go very slowly.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-04-96 \par \par \uc2  1009GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds4o03giv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
