\par\par \b \uc2  BULGARIAN LEV FALLS TO ALL-TIME LOW OF 91 VS DLR. \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SOFIA, April 24 (Reuter) - The Bulgarian lev shed 3.4 percent on Wednesday to close at an all-time low of 91.00 per dollar due to very low supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We sold a small amount of dollars at 91 levs in late afternoon," a commercial bank dealer said, adding that a demand for some $1.5 million by the same buyer had remained unsatisfied by the close. \par \par \uc2  The local branch of a foreign bank has actively bid for dollars throughout the day, attracting the scarce offers at increasingly higher lev rates, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Most banks, worried by the sharp lev fall, refrained from trading in the market and preferred to strike deals mainly with final clients, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Traders have lost confidence in each other after \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade was disrupted earlier this week by cancellation of forward contracts," another commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  At least two financial brokerages have cancelled payments since last week on forward contracts, putting banks with short dollar positions in a difficult situation. \par \par \uc2  This pushed most banks out of the market, which in turn made trade very thin and volatile with the bid/ask spread widening to three to four levs. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not sighted trading in the market, dealers said, adding that shrinking \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and uncertainty over funding deals with the international lending institutions continue to weigh heavily on the lev. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $201 million to $703 million in March. They stood at $1.3 billion in December before Bulgaria had to make Brady coupon interest payments, interest payments to the Paris Club of creditor governments and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the lev. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to pay a total of $1.2 billion on its foreign debt this year. This is expected to stretch Sofia's finances to the limit if it fails to strike fresh funding deals with the International Monetary Fund and the World Bank, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The IMF and the World Bank are currently scrutinising the small print of a reform programme handed over by Bulgaria's socialist government nearly two weeks ago. -- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-328101 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040127ds4o008ud\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
