\par\par \b \uc2  Bulgarian lev recovers to 83.00 vs dlr at close. \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SOFIA, April 18 (Reuter) - A moderate rise of dollar supply helped the Bulgarian lev recover to around 83.00 per dollar at the close of the interbank market on Thursday, from its record low of 83.70 in late morning trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "A large commercial bank offered a relatively small amount of dollars in early afternoon at levels around 83.00 levs and the market settled there until the close," a commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Low supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to market worries over a sharp fall in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and uncertainty whether Bulgaria will strike much-needed funding deals with the IMF and the World Bank pressured the lev, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "In a market as thin as today's every dip in supply or demand brings large volatility," another commercial bank dealer said after the lev weakened to 83.70 per dollar two hours after opening around 82.50. \par \par \uc2  The lev closed at 81.60 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Under \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  preliminary estimates \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have fallen to $720 million in March from $1.27 billion at the end of 1995 following interest payments on \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commercial and official foreign debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the lev. \par \par \uc2  -- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-328101 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds4i095mq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
