\par\par \b \uc2  Bulgaria  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves fall to $703 million. \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SOFIA, April 18 (Reuter) - Bulgaria's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $703 million at the end of March from $904 million a month earlier, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Lyubomir Filipov said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "At the end of last month the reserves stood at $703 million," Filipov told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "In the last few weeks we have bought $46 million," he said, adding that commercial banks had withdrawn some $30 million from their obligatory \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits and had not offered them on the market. \par \par \uc2  By June commercial banks must transfer their dollar-denominated minimum required reserves into levs, which will bring dollars onto the market, Filipov said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to buy the dollars offered and thus to increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  Filipov said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would rely on these dollars and on export earnings as well as its reserves to meet Brady coupon interest and other debt payments due in July. \par \par \uc2  Bulgaria's reserves have fallen from $1.3 billion since last December because of Brady coupon interest payments in January, interest payments to the Paris Club of official creditors and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the lev. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty over whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria\b0 \highlight\uc2  will clinch funding deals with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and the World Bank have contributed to the downward pressure on the lev. \par \par \uc2  Keen to raise cash to cover this year's foreign debt payments totalling $1.2 billion, the government last week submitted a detailed reform plan to the two funding institutions. @ \par \par \uc2  Bulgaria's failure to meet reform targets -- including closing down loss-making state firms and restructuring its debt-laden banking sector -- has postponed funding agreements with the lending institutions for two years in a row. \par \par \uc2  A World Bank mission is currently visiting Sofia. \par \par \uc2  Filipov told reporters an IMF mission was expected in the Bulgarian capital early in May. -- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-328101 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds4i095k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
