\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central bank \highlight\uc2  buying pushes up  \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria \highlight\uc2  lev - dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SOFIA, Feb 21 (Reuter) - Large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped push up the Bulgarian lev to 75.15/20 per dollar at the close on the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, well above the opening 75.40, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Massive dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning calmed down the market and strengthened the lev," a commercial bank dealer said. Operators said trade was active as many banks sought dollars for final clients and building of long positions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched dollar sales in early trade for the second day in a row to halt the lev fall. No details of the amounts sold were available. \par \par \uc2  The lev weakened to around 76.20 yesterday morning and seemed headed for a further fall before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began. \par \par \uc2  Trade on the interbank money market was rather dull and thin as few banks offered lev funds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  According to traders, banks with free levs channelled them to the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which further curbed supply to the money market. The interbank depo rate was flat on Tuesday's 45.4-45.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-328101 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2l017xz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
