\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Bulgaria \highlight\uc2  Sold -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervened \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 15:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The stronger lev on Tuesday's interbank market followed a sharp drop by lev against the dollar on Monday, according to the state news agency BTA. \par \par \uc2  BTA quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Todor Valchev as saying that a moderate climb for the dollar is normal against the lev, given the increase in Bulgarian inflation of around 10% from January to March. \par \par \uc2  But Valchev added that it's important for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to control \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions and warned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in a better position now against speculation than last year. Valchev said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $6 million on the interbank market Tuesday and sold $20 million to the government. \par \par \uc2  BTA quoted dealers as saying that they expect the lev's exchange rate to be influence in coming days by the introduction of the 1995 budget. Even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market became more lively, demand for debt at Monday's and last Firday's auctions exceeded the supply, according to the National Bank. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1414GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3f01vwt\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalp